<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lango</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lango sub-region</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lango is a region of northern Uganda north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-kyoga">Lake Kyoga</a>, home of the Lango people, who speak a Luo language. In the nineteenth century it lay beyond the borders of the kingdoms and served as a refuge for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabalega">Kabalega</a> during his war against the British; he and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwanga-ii">Mwanga II</a> were captured there in April 1899. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milton-obote">Milton Obote</a>, Uganda's first prime minister, came from Lango.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lango.jpg" alt="Lango" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kirk979 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lango_subregion.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
